    "done_when": "tests/test_sub_floor_dimension_is_an_obligation.py stores two reviews in a temporary config home. One has totals of 78 or 79 with durability 5, the section's measured pair. The other has every dimension at or above its floor. The test asserts that the obligations report carries a sub-floor row for the first, naming the run, the dimension, the score and the floor, and no such row for the second. It asserts that after a recorded disposition the row no longer appears. It asserts that the floor is read from flight config: changing the configured floor in the test's flight file moves the verdict.\n\nThe test fails at the base revision (logged) and passes at the head. The negative control makes the obligations reader ignore dimensions in a scratch copy, and the first review then produces no row, with the mutation on the red log's first line.\n\nThe regenerated schema artefacts match a fresh regeneration from the committed flight.yaml source.\n\nThe gate is the new test plus the existing obligations and flight-schema tests. It exits 0, or shows no added failing ids against the base, with both arms recorded as log paths under baseline_suite and after_suite. The test neither reads nor writes the real ~/.config/reckon.",
    "estimated_hours": 4.0,
    "goal": "Plan crew-observability-truth §21. Read the section in docs/plans/crew-observability-truth.html, in particular its measure \"A dimension below its floor is not averaged away\". A review's five dimension scores are parsed and stored, and nothing reads them back. A total of 78 carrying a durability of 5 promotes as cleanly as a 95.\n\nMake a stored review dimension that is below its floor surface as a finding that requires a disposition. The finding is an obligation row that reckon/crew/obligations.py reports for the session until it is disposed, never averaged into the total. The floor is per dimension and is declared in flight config, beside the other gate settings (the reckon/schema/flight.yaml source plus its regenerated _flight_schema.py and flight.schema.json, and a shipped default in flight-defaults.yaml), not compiled in.\n\nChoose the disposition vocabulary to match the section's closed set: folded with a node id, or exempted with a recorded reason. Keep it minimal. The section's other measures (per-role rubric, actor ownership, queryable joins) are out of scope for this node.",
